                        <h1>Crop Enterprise Budgets for Arkansas</h1>
                        
                        <h2>2026-7 Arkansas Crop Enterprise Budgets</h2>
                        
                        <p>The crop enterprise budgets are made possible thanks to support from check-off funds
                           administered by the Arkansas Corn and Grain Sorghum Board, Arkansas Rice Research
                           and Promotion Board, and Arkansas Soybean Promotion Board as well as the University
                           of Arkansas Division of Agriculture.</p>
                        
                        <p><img title="Arkansas Corn and Grain Sorghum Board logo" src="/farm-ranch/economics-marketing/farm-planning/budgets/images/ARC_GSB-Logo.png" alt="Arkansas Corn and Grain Sorghum Board logo" width="233" height="60"> &nbsp;<img title="Arkansas Rice Research and Promotion Board logo" src="/farm-ranch/economics-marketing/farm-planning/budgets/images/ricepromotionboardlogoRPBlogo-1-300x173.png" alt="Arkansas Rice Research and Promotion Board logo" width="169" height="97"> &nbsp;<img title="Arkansas Soybean Promotion Board logo" src="/farm-ranch/economics-marketing/farm-planning/budgets/images/aspb_logo_300.png" alt="Arkansas Soybean Promotion Board logo" width="208" height="83"></p>
                        
                        <p style="text-align: left;">The crop enterprise budgets and calculator are developed by Breana Watkins, Instructor
                           with the Agricultural Economics and Agribusiness Department (AEAB).&nbsp;</p>
                        
                        <p><a class="noxlsxicon" title="2026 Farm Machinery and Equipment Costs per Acre" href="/farm-ranch/economics-marketing/farm-planning/budgets/farm_equipment_2026.xlsx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2026 Farm Machinery and Equipment Costs per Acre</a></p>
                        
                        <h3>Last updated August 26, 2026</h3>
                        
                        <p>*2027 wheat budget released</p>
                        
                        <p>*2027 canola - new budget available below; please contact Scott Stiles (<a href="mailto:sstiles@uada.edu">sstiles@uada.edu</a>) for more information.</p>
                        
